Title: Great Britain's Oliver Rowland wins Formula E title in Germany
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Oliver Rowland', 'Text': '"Honestly, I was just thinking before the race not to have too much damage going into [the final round in] London," said Rowland.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 93}}, {'Speaker': 'Oliver Rowland', 'Text': '"I can\'t believe it, I have no words. It\'s incredible. I was trying to play it safe but everybody was so aggressive, so at some point I was all in.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 142}}, {'Speaker': 'Oliver Rowland', 'Text': '"Thankfully I stayed out of trouble."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 33}}], 'Description': [{'Description': "Great Britain's Oliver Rowland has secured the Formula E title for the first time after a fourth place finish in Berlin, Germany.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 97}}, {'Description': 'The Nissan driver won the championship with two races to spare and becomes the 10th different champion in 11 seasons.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 107}}, {'Description': "Porsche's Pascal Wehrlein was Rowland's closest title rival, but the German slipped down to 16th in Sunday's race despite starting on pole at Berlin's old Tempelhof airport.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 108, 'EndChar': 247}}, {'Description': 'He has 184 points going into the final two races of the season in London (26-27 July), while Wehrlein sits on 125.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 110}}, {'Description': "Jaguar's Nick Cassidy won Sunday's race as Jake Dennis (Andretti) finished second and Jean-Eric Vergne (DS Penske) came home in third.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 116}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Oliver Rowland'}]}
